<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Indochina War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1946">1946</a>–<a href="/years/1954">1954</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochina">Indochina</a> War was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a>, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh">Ho Chi Minh</a>, after France tried to restore its rule over Indochina following the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. The Viet Minh, aided from 1950 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, defeated the French at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dien-bien-phu">Dien Bien Phu</a> in 1954. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> Accords then ended French Indochina and divided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> at the 17th parallel.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-indochina-war.jpg" alt="First Indochina War" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mohamed Ajjani · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:First_Indochina_War_COLLAGE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
